\subsection{Energy Conservation Residual Enforcement Gate}

To satisfy the Blackwell Hamiltonian Encryption Theorem under continuous operation,
the system evaluates global Hamiltonian residuals at every discrete timestep $\Delta t$:
\begin{equation}
\frac{\big|H(t_{\text{final}})-H(t_{0})\big|}
     {H(t_{0})}
< 10^{-12}.
\end{equation}
If thermal noise or boundary turbulence causes the energy residual to approach this threshold,
adaptive Runge--Kutta--Fehlberg timestep throttling,
\begin{equation}
\Delta t \rightarrow \mathcal{O}(\Delta t^{p}),
\end{equation}
automatically engages to lock state-vector propagation and prevent numerical divergence.